econds, i.e. no shortfall. POL-NS-03 is closed: the driver was stationary inside the arrival radius (nearest approach 28.8 m), not outside it, so the 400 m wrong-entrance test is not reached.\n\nThe fee is correct. Under the fee schedule's resolution rule the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 8.00 RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee is SGD 8.00, which is exactly the line itemised in EV-FARE-00208 (difference 0.00), so there is no billing defect under POL-NS-08(d).\n\nPOL-NS-07 therefore applies in full: the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the SGD 8.00 cancellation fee, being SGD 6.40, and the anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and the ratio against 143 completed trips in 30 days is 0.014 (below 0.08); both limbs are required and neither fires. Your SGD 8.00 charge stands as it presently is; the SGD 6.40 is paid to the driver by the platform, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries that same figure because this is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling.\n\nOn the two remaining points: the rider's prior_no_show_flags of 3 is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 lists as context only and it carries no ground of decision either way; the trailing-window rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below the 3 threshold) and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, so no escalation on abuse grounds under POL-NS-09(c) or (d) arises. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00208-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and carries no fact; no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) was needed on a single unbroken run, so its absence changes nothing. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d), and your request for a call is noted but no clause produces a referral on these facts.\n\nConfidence is 0.95, capped at 1.0 because every artifact carrying the deciding facts (EV-GPS-00208, EV-TRIP-00208, EV-FARE-00208) has weight 1.0."
